																		An in-universe parody of Are We Cool Yet.
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/blither" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5614757); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5614757&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609856760" alt="Blither" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5614757)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/blither" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5614757); return false;" >Blither</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609575163 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Jan 2021 08:12</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4860096">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<p>-Anomalous statue with &quot;Are We Cool Yet&quot; carved into the bottom. Occasionally 'activates', creating a memetic aura causing a variety of effects in people around them. Note attached, filled with nonsensical writing &quot;explaining&quot; the artistic significance of the statue. The effects are assumed by the Foundation to be some kind of pretentious commentary, as most AWCY projects are, and try to figure out what it all means in an attempt to stop its effects or discover its creator.</p>
<p>-Is eventually revealed to be an in-universe parody of AWCY, likely made by a member of ACWY as a sort of self-own after it stops its effects and is reclassified as neutralised.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<p>-Foundation attempts to interpret the effects of the statue, researching increasingly obscure art pieces and reaching more and more in an attempt to work out what the artist was trying to say.</p>
<p>-One of the statues effects makes the researchers think the statue is prophesying some catastrophic event, fuelled by their own (justified, at this point) paranoia, and begin kidnapping and interrogating AWCY members to no avail.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>-Their interpretations become ridiculously complex in a search for some kind of cohesive meaning, matching the actual effects of the statue becoming more nonsensical and racking up a larger body count in the process. Eventually the statue starts just killing people at random for seemingly no reason, before stopping completely.</p>
<p>-Item is reclassified as &quot;Safe&quot; or &quot;neutralized&quot; and the foundation eventually works out that they have inadvertently been led on a wild goose chase, and deduce the item was meant as a parody of AWCY themselves- meaningless effects resulting in unnecessarily deaths and a note pretentiously explaining the work.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong></p>
<p>-The items effects are extremely weird and nonsensical, and the foundation's interpretations of the items effects cross-link other SCP's and reference various societal or historical events, phenomenon, and art pieces.</p>
<p>-As far as I could tell there aren't any AWCY scips that directly make fun of their own group, which seems something right up their alley.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<p>-Started as a GAW project, but I prefer it as an actual AWCY member making fun of the group he's apart of.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
