			<div class="content" id="post-content-4862770">
									

<p>I should make it clear that the article itself isn't meant to be a parody, in-universe it's just a regular foundation document like any other. The statue itself is a disillusioned AWCY creating something to mock AWCY. Essentially saying they're all just psychopaths making harmful objects and justifying it with a bunch of bullshit about creating 'art'. I don't picture the artist responsible as trying to be funny really, but mocking the organisation he is/was apart of.</p>
<p>Now that I think about it, it's sort of the reverse of -1802, the AWCY robot that makes fun of the foundation.</p>
<p>And I do realise now that the concept does make the foundation look pretty incompetent. I think the statue killing one or two people before the foundation ramps up its precautions would fit a lot better, and for there to be a solid reason why the foundation tries to find out what the piece is saying. I'm currently mulling over what exactly convinces the foundation to try and 'interpret' the work rather than lock it away completely, and I'm thinking maybe it's just the one senior researcher who has a background in anomalous art and becomes obsessed with the piece, perhaps his personal notes are the things being partially logged in the article.</p>
<p>As to your second-last paragraph @cybersqyd - that sounds like a really interesting SCP idea for a much better writer than me, I don't think my ability extends to deep-dive analysis of art history.</p>

							</div>

								
					
