					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fireknight" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5930130); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5930130&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609856760" alt="Fireknight" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5930130)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fireknight" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5930130); return false;" >Fireknight</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609707283 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Jan 2021 20:54</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4861423">
									

<p>I like the concept of an AWCY parody, it certainly feels like something they’d do. But at the same time this doesn’t seem much like a parody. Most of what I’m seeing here is various tropes collecting together. You have unnecessary violence:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Eventually the statue starts just killing people at random for seemingly no reason, before stopping completely.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You have the cruel Foundation:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>kidnapping and interrogating AWCY members</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Tropes are all well and good for parodies. But my problem is that if I were reading this, I wouldn’t think, “neat, this person’s parodying various SCP tropes.” I would think, “why is this such a cliche SCP?” I think the main problem is that you have inconsistent abilities for the statue. With the strange set of powers you’ve given it I see no good way for you to properly explain to the reader that the researcher’s behavior is caused by the statue.</p>
<p>Overall, I like the idea of a parody SCP like this and you seem to be on the right track. But I think you’d face significant problems when trying to communicate the idea to the reader with the properties you’re using now.</p>

							</div>

								
					
