				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609856760" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;" >cybersqyd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609750572 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">04 Jan 2021 08:56</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4861726">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>matching the actual effects of the statue becoming more nonsensical and racking up a larger body count in the process. Eventually the statue starts just killing people at random for seemingly no reason</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm a little hesitant about this aspect because like&#8230;.it feels like the Foundation should be better equipped to handle this?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the foundation eventually works out that they have inadvertently been led on a wild goose chase, and deduce the item was meant as a parody of AWCY themselves</p>
</blockquote>
<p>this feels&#8230;perhaps odd to me; like&#8230;I kinda get how this works as a parody of AWCY? but it feels like, the whole angle of it leading the foundation on a wild goose chase feels like the actual parody angle of the object is too subtle in universe: like, generally if you're doing a parody, you want people to know it's a parody and enjoy it as such; rather than to trick them into reacting like it's real right up until you pull the curtain back and go 'sike', y'know?</p>
<p>Part of me also feels like the Foundation is a lot more likely to ask 'how do we get this to stop' than 'what is the artist trying to say' and I'm a little unsure of the focus here as a result.</p>
<p>I think there's a small part of me that feels like doing a genuinely confusing artistic piece sincerely; like, the kind of anart piece that genuinely defies meaning and which the foundation attempts to understand the why of might be more interesting than treating it as a parody of AWCY?; and like, having this as an exploration of what art is would be more interesting but *shrugs*.</p>
<p>Alternatively: the idea of this being a thing to make fun of AWCY? feels actually fun and I think taking this in a lot more comedic route could help; where like, instead of being just 'a bunch of actual AWCY? things slapped together weirdly', it's like, a deliberately incompetently done piece? Where you actually like, play up the comedy a lot more and deliberately make this a funny article about a weird thing: like almost using the classic comedy duo thing of the SCP being the comedy provider and the Foundation being the straight man, y'know?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

